Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:36:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Vulkan FG input: retry the SR carrier hook instead of
 refusing for the session

NGX briefly maps the game folder's nvngx_dlss.dll while the bridge creates its
private feature, and the bridge's own NGX module scanner keeps it mapped until
its hooks there are installed. When that scan is slow, the carrier search sees
two DLSS SR modules, correctly declines the ambiguous hook, and NR stayed off
for the whole session (a resolution change recovered it).

- Classify carrier failures: no unique SR module, an SR module that could not
  be retained, and MinHook status 9 are transient; everything else is fatal.
- Keep the private session built and owned while the carrier is pending; arm
  and process no frame; retry once per second, up to 30 attempts, then refuse
  as before. An ambiguous carrier is still never hooked.
- Log the module list on the first and last attempt only; name the module the
  hook was installed on; clear the SR/hook diagnostic on success.
- Tests: run.cmd carrier (fixture SR/RR modules, production search, MinHook
  install, retry step, relay guard); run.cmd racehelper builds a test-only
  add-on that recreates the race in a game.
